<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35576" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔνθεος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, in
		later Prose 
			contr.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔνθους</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			Ph.
			2.542
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			App.
			<u>Hisp.</u>
			18
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Aen.Gaz.
			<u>Thphr.</u>
			p.12
		</span></i>
		<i><span class="en">
			B.
		</span></i>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>full of the
				god, inspired, possessed,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔ. γυναῖκες,</span> of the Bacchantes,
				<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				964
			</span></i> (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔ. Ἄρει</span>
			<i>possessed</i> by him, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				497
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ Πανός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hipp.</u>
					141
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ τοῦ ἔρωτος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Smp.</u>
					1.10
				</span></i>
			: c. gen. rei, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέχνης νιν Ζεὺς ἔνθεον κτίσας φρένα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Eu.</u>
					17
				</span></i>
			; also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔ. πρὸς ἀρετήν</span>
			<i>inspired with a love for</i> it, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Smp.</u>
				179a
			</span></i>: 
				Sup.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ωτάτη, φύσις,</span> of Homer, <i><span class="en">
				Max.
			</span></i> Tyr.<i><span class="en">
				32.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of divine
			frenzy, <i>inspired by the god,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέχναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					1209
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαντική</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Phdr.</u>
					244b
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαντεῖαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ti.</u>
					72b
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔνθεον ἡ ποίησις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					1408b19
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔ. φιλία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.752c
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ἔ.</span>
			<i>frenzied rites,</i> prob.in <i><span class="en">
				Herod.
				8.70
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνθέως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Men.
					<u>Mon.</u>
					229
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				App.
				<u>Hisp.</u>
				26
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Jul.
				<u>Or.</u>
				7.215b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Iamb.
				<u>VP</u>
				32.216
			</span></i>.</div>
